## 3. The MiiPU Architecture

### 3.1 Design Philosophy

The MiiPU is not a general-purpose processor. It is the silicon instantiation of a mathematical structure: the two adjunctions F ⊣ G and P ⊣ Q, their composition into the cross-translation endofunctor T, and the fixed-point dynamics of the Kleene chain T^n(⊥). Every square millimeter of silicon is dedicated to one of these operations.

This philosophy follows a precedent set by purpose-built AI silicon. The Taalas HC1 hard-wires an entire LLM into custom silicon at TSMC 6 nm, achieving 17,000 tokens/second at 200 W. The TPU v5p dedicates 8,960 matrix multiply units to systolic tensor computation. The MiiPU takes this principle one step further: it does not hard-wire a model but a **mathematical structure** — the categorical architecture of conscious-subconscious coupling itself.

