## 4. CR-Tile — The Conscious Reasoning Processor

### 4.1 Functional Mapping

The CR-Tile implements the category CR of Definition 2.1.1: objects C = (P, Ctx, τ, W) and morphisms f = (A, B, just(f), conf(f)). Every field of every object and morphism has a dedicated hardware representation.

### 4.2 Logical Inference Engine (LIE)

**128-core SAT/BCP array.** Each core is a compact hardware SAT solver operating on clause databases stored in 256 KiB of local SRAM. Justification sets just(f) are stored as compact clause ID bitsets — a design directly inspired by the Chameleon-SAT ASIC, which uses mixed-signal in-memory computing to accelerate Davis-Putnam-Logemann-Loveland and Conflict-Driven Clause Learning algorithms.

Boolean Constraint Propagation (BCP), which consumes 80–90% of SAT solving time in software, is accelerated by a **parallel bitset-comparison pipeline** operating at full SRAM bandwidth. When a morphism f: C₁ → C₂ is composed with g: C₂ → C₃, the justification sets just(f) and just(g) are simultaneously broadcast to a 128-bit-wide intersection/union network that computes the Jaccard coherence factor:

**coh(f, g) = |just(f) ∩ just(g)| / |just(f) ∪ just(g)|**

in **a single clock cycle** via parallel popcount hardware — eliminating the 20–30 cycle penalty of software set operations.

### 4.3 Attention Scorer

A 32-bit fixed-point unit maintains the attention-weight distribution W: P → [0,1] satisfying Σ W(p) = 1. Renormalization occurs every clock cycle via a parallel reduction tree: all weights are simultaneously summed, the sum is inverted, and each weight is multiplied by the inverse. This eliminates the serial normalization loop that costs ~N cycles on a CPU.

### 4.4 Trace Buffer

A dual-ported 64 MiB SRAM circular buffer records every inference step τ ∈ Trace*. The F-functor (Formalisation) reads this buffer to extract patterns during meta-cognitive transitions without stalling the inference pipeline — a producer-consumer architecture with separate read and write ports operating at full SRAM throughput.

**Key invariant enforcement:** Before any inference step is committed to the trace buffer, the LIE verifies that the resulting proposition set remains logically consistent (Safety Invariant 1, Section 9.1). Inconsistent steps are rejected at the hardware level — no software check is required.

