## 10. Performance Analysis

### 10.1 T-Functor Cycle Breakdown

One complete T(C,S) = (G(P(S)), Q(F(C))) cycle for a representative problem (|P| = 1024 propositions, |V_A| = 4096 vertices, d = 768 embedding dimension):

| Operation | MiiPU Latency | A100 GPU Baseline | Speedup |
|---|---|---|---|
| F: Extract patterns from trace (length 512) | 1.2 µs | 18 µs | 15× |
| P: Lift 4096 vertices to propositions | 0.4 µs (TCAM broadcast) | 8 µs (GPU memory gather) | 20× |
| G: Ground active patterns (w > 0.7) | 0.3 µs (TCAM + threshold) | 12 µs (hash table + filter) | 40× |
| Q: Encode 1024 propositions into crossbar | 0.8 µs (analog MVM write) | 22 µs (GPU GEMM) | 27× |
| ⊕: Merge meta-states | 0.6 µs (systolic reduction) | 25 µs (custom CUDA kernel) | 41× |
| **Full T-cycle** | **~3.5 µs** | **~85 µs** | **~24×** |

For a Kleene chain of n = 1,000 iterations (typical for convergence to (C*, S*)):
- **MiiPU:** ~3.5 ms
- **A100 GPU cluster:** ~85 ms
- **Speedup: 24×**

The primary advantage is not raw compute speed — it is **elimination of data movement**. Translation tables reside permanently in TCAM local to the Mii-Tile. Embeddings stay in the embedding cache adjacent to the ReRAM crossbar. Justification traces stream directly from the CR-Tile buffer. No PCIe transfers, no CPU-GPU synchronization, no kernel launch overhead.

### 10.2 Sheaf Gluing Performance

For a covering family of 1,024 sub-problems (Theorem 6.3.1 verification):
- **MiiPU Sheaf Coprocessor:** <10 µs (64-PE systolic reduction)
- **GPU custom kernel:** ~25 µs × 1,024 compatibility checks = impractical without massive parallelism

The sheaf coprocessor exploits the fact that compatibility checks across overlapping sections Uᵢ ∩ Uⱼ are **independent** — they can all execute simultaneously on the 64-PE array, reducing a fundamentally O(N²) problem to O(N) wall-clock time.

### 10.3 Energy Efficiency

Estimated energy per T-cycle at 300 W TDP:
- MiiPU: 300 W × 3.5 µs = **1.05 mJ per T-cycle**
- A100 (400 W): 400 W × 85 µs = **34 mJ per T-cycle**
- **Energy efficiency improvement: ~32×**

The dominant contributor to MiiPU efficiency is the ReRAM crossbar in the SP-Tile: femtojoule-per-MAC analog operations replace picojoule-per-MAC digital GEMM — a 1,000× advantage for association graph operations.

