## 11. Implementation Roadmap

### Phase 1 — FPGA Prototype (Now → 12 Months)

**Target hardware:** Xilinx Alveo U55C or Intel Agilex 7 with HBM2e.

**Scope:** All five functional units (LIE, H-CAM, TTE, Sheaf Coprocessor, FPC) implemented as RTL on FPGA fabric. The ReRAM crossbar is replaced by a digital SRAM-based simulation of the analog operations (SRAM-based IMC), preserving the functional interface while deferring the analog challenge to Phase 2.

**Toolchain:** NSFlow (IBM Research, DAC 2025) provides the FPGA substrate for neurosymbolic dataflow. The MiiPU-specific units (Adjunction Unit, Sheaf Gluing Logic, Kleene Chain Controller) are developed as NSFlow extensions using HLS (High-Level Synthesis) via Xilinx Vitis or Intel OpenCL.

**Open-source stack:** Chisel3 for RTL design; Verilator for simulation; RISC-V custom extensions implemented via the CFU Playground framework; NSFlow for dataflow substrate; OpenROAD for initial floorplan exploration.

**Deliverables:** Working FPGA prototype executing the full T-functor cycle; benchmark results against GPU baseline; ISA compliance tests for all MiiISA instructions; SVA formal properties for the three safety invariants.

### Phase 2 — ASIC Tape-Out (12–36 Months)

**Target process:** TSMC N4 FinFET for CR-Tile and Mii-Tiles; TSMC N4 with analog BEOL extension for SP-Tile ReRAM crossbar.

**Packaging:** TSMC CoWoS Gen 6 silicon interposer with UCIe 3.0 links and 4× HBM4 stacks.

**Critical path:** The ReRAM crossbar is the primary fabrication risk. IBM's CMO/HfOₓ platform has demonstrated 4-bit precision (>32 stable states) with acceptable drift at 130 nm node. The conservative fallback is a digital SRAM-based CIM (Compute-in-Memory) array at lower energy efficiency but equivalent functionality and significantly de-risked fabrication.

**TSMC shuttle access:** For academic institutions, TSMC's Multi-Project Wafer (MPW) shuttle via MOSIS or CMP provides access to N28 initially, scaling toward N7/N4 for production designs. Google's OpenMPW program supports open-source designs at 130 nm → 90 nm for initial validation.

**Formal verification:** Full SVA verification of all three safety invariants using Cadence JasperGold. Gate-level simulation of the complete T-functor pipeline. Power analysis using Cadence Voltus.

### Phase 3 — Production Silicon: Mii Intelligence Unit (MIU) (36–60 Months)

**Target process:** TSMC N3 or N2 for peak energy efficiency; CoWoS Gen 6/7 packaging with 8× HBM4 stacks.

**Performance target:** Full T-cycle in <1 µs at N2; Kleene chain of 10,000 iterations in <10 ms; Sheaf gluing of 65,536 sub-problems in <100 µs.

**The native ISA is complete and frozen at Phase 1.** The MIU is binary-compatible with Phase 1 FPGA implementations — the same programs run on both, with the ASIC providing the target performance.

