## 13. Conclusion

The Mii Logical Architecture is not a software framework running on commodity hardware. It is a **hardware specification** — a blueprint whose mathematical primitives map one-to-one to silicon functional units. The two adjunctions F ⊣ G and P ⊣ Q define the TTE's bidirectional lookup semantics. The cross-translation functor T defines the MiiISA's ITERATE instruction. The sheaf condition of Theorem 6.3.1 defines the Sheaf Coprocessor's equalizer pipeline. The Kleene Fixed-Point Theorem defines the FPC's convergence state machine.

Just as GPUs crystallize the algebra of linear transformations in silicon, and neuromorphic chips crystallize the dynamics of spiking neurons, the MiiPU crystallizes the **categorical structure of cognition itself** — the adjunctions, the sheaves, the Kleene chains — as a native computational substrate.

Any system that operates through the adjunctions F ⊣ G and P ⊣ Q becomes a native workload for this processor. The MiiPU does not accelerate a model. It accelerates a **way of thinking**.

